listing_content:
Jean-Pierre Filippini is a true embodiment of an innovative and people-centric leader. His sterling record showcases a profound understanding of commercial strategies and a commitment to producing results. His passion for integral leadership extends beyond merely setting goals; he creates a conducive environment that allows individual talents to flourish. He treats every challenge as an opportunity for innovation, bringing forth fresh and unconventional perspectives. But perhaps his greatest strength is in coaching. He is not just a guide; he is a mentor, providing a second opinion that is steeped in years of experience and wisdom. His hands-on approach to nurturing growth, development and success is truly inspiring. Filippini's style of leadership is unique and impactful. When he gives a second opinion, you know it's backed by a rich reservoir of knowledge and insight.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=72]

Inge Van Belle, with her unique blend of 12+ years in start-ups/scale-ups and 10+ years of corporate experience in business consulting, PR, B2B sales, and marketing, primarily in ICT, is an expert in employee engagement and corporate culture. As a former Director of Communications, she applied her skills during the merger of Telindus and Proximus, further cementing her expertise. Having led employee experience projects in 10 countries, she has validated theoretical knowledge with practical experience, specializing in the 12 drivers of employee engagement and organisational culture.

As a Co-Founder of Herculean Alliance, she's committed to addressing the challenges of employee disconnection in hybrid work environments. Her book, “Employee Engagement, what else?” co-authored with Klaus Lommatzsch, is a testament to her mission. Also, her work as a strategic advisor to Dubai Police and as a keynote speaker for the United Nations Women underscores her authority in the field.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=57]

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Gino Geysermans is a sales expert with over 20 years of experience in different sales and management roles. He has led both sales and pre-sales teams primarily in Large Enterprise. Experience matter expert in integrating sales teams post acquisition,steering teams through times of change and sales enablement. He is human-oriented and contagious in his enthusiasm. He tends to bring out the best in people and make teams perform above expectation. He believes in strengthening the stronger skills than focus on the less developed ones.

&nbsp;

He is open-minded, discreet and professional which makes it easy for him to win over people. Establishing trustworthy and sustainable relations, both with colleagues and customers is second nature.

Being a translator his communication skills help to build bridges and clearly communicate. His ability to empathize with people and his overall interest in different cultures have often made it easy for him to mediate and anticipate.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=45]

'The common thread throughout my activities is building a sustainable well-being policy. With a focus on the interaction between physical and mental health, combined with the acquisition of the right skills, I am an expert in my domain. My passion is to empower organizations, teams, and individuals, helping them to become resilient and harness their strengths. As an expert in business-related matters, Griet is the perfect person to provide a second opinion and help guide decisions towards success.'

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=30]

Jan Paesen is a great expert to provide a second opinion because of his <strong>25+ years professional experience</strong> in a wide variety of industries such as Banking, Manufacturing, Consultancy Services, and Telecom. He has worked in different domains such as Finance, IT, Product Management, Solution Sales, and Marketing. He has also worked in companies of different sizes ranging from startups to big corporate organizations. Jan Paesen has held different roles in his career ranging from Analyst to VP/Director Exco -1 in a ‘Bel20’ listed company.

His key experience areas include Strategic Marketing, Digital &amp; Content Marketing, Branding &amp; Communication, Product Management &amp; Go-To-Market, Program &amp; Project Management, Team Facilitation / People / Change Mgt, Budgeting &amp; Forecasting, Business Case / Financial Modelling, Vendor / Partnership Management, Business Development / Strategy &amp; Innovation.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=75]

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Jackie Janssen is a great expert to provide a second opinion because of his passion for helping individuals and teams in their development. He combines fun, improvement and inspiration to achieve results and has a personal passion for blending his outside interests into his career. He is a public speaker and entertrainer who loves to twist the minds of his audience. His specialisms include ICT development , Data Management, hands-on use of AI

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=56]

Remy Knecht is a <strong>Chief Security Officer</strong> at itsmeDigitalID. He has a special interest in Digital Identity, Cyber Security and Digital Transformation. <a class='tooltip-target' data-citationid='e2cd0f0f-2f44-e963-3fb6-2fafad55726b-7-group'>He is also an expert in Digital ID World Economic Forum</a><a class='ac-anchor sup-target' href='https://be.linkedin.com/posts/remyknecht_giac-security-operations-manager-gsom-was-activity-6950549339173752832-gSLG' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-citationid='e2cd0f0f-2f44-e963-3fb6-2fafad55726b-7' aria-label='Remy Knecht on LinkedIn: GIAC Security Operations Manager (GSOM) was ...'><sup>2</sup></a>. He has been a partner at Flying Forward 2020<a class='tooltip-target' data-citationid='e2cd0f0f-2f44-e963-3fb6-2fafad55726b-11-group'> and a director at Digie</a><a class='ac-anchor sup-target' href='https://be.linkedin.com/posts/remyknecht_giac-security-operations-manager-gsom-was-activity-6950549339173752832-gSLG' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-citationid='e2cd0f0f-2f44-e963-3fb6-2fafad55726b-11' aria-label='Remy Knecht on LinkedIn: GIAC Security Operations Manager (GSOM) was ...'><sup>2</sup></a>. He has been recognized as an industry expert by FATF and Cyber Sec Expert EU CyberNet. <a class='tooltip-target' data-citationid='e2cd0f0f-2f44-e963-3fb6-2fafad55726b-17-group'>He is also a member of GIAC Advisory Board - GSEC</a>

&nbsp;

Based on his experience and expertise, Remy Knecht can provide a second opinion on topics related to Digital Identity, Cyber Security and Digital Transformation.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=73]

Frank van der Ent is a great expert to provide a second opinion because of his extensive experience in commercial strategy, go-to-market strategy, consolidation or integration process, growth or scale-up phase, business development, and mergers and acquisitions. He has a track record in general and commercial management positions in both corporate and smaller organizations. He is result-driven with a strong financial basis and an energetic team builder with the ability to align various interests from technical, operational, and commercial perspectives. His focus is not limited to the telecommunications and ICT industry in Belgium and the Netherlands. Based on his experience, he has the ability to analyze, define a strategy or solution, and execute.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=37]

Tom Schuyten is a great expert to provide a second opinion because he has a wealth of experience in software development and education. He is a co-founder of Gift2Give and Plugin2Drive, which are both software development companies that specialize in creating innovative solutions for their clients. He is also a lecturer at PXL, where he teaches students about software development. Tom Schuyten has a strong background in Java and backend Spring development, which makes him an expert in these fields. Additionally, he is an Atlassian enthusiast, which means he has extensive knowledge of Atlassian products. His experience and expertise make him an excellent choice for providing a second opinion on software development projects.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=58]

Sam Bruynseels is an expert in his field with years of experience and a proven track record. He has worked with some of the biggest names in the industry and has a wealth of knowledge that he can draw upon to provide a second opinion. Sam’s expertise is not just limited to his former employers, but extends to all areas of his field. He is passionate about what he does and is always looking for ways to improve and innovate. Sam’s ability to think outside the box and come up with creative solutions is what sets him apart from others in his field. If you’re looking for someone who can provide a fresh perspective and valuable insights, then Sam Bruynseels is the expert you need.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=76]

Elizabeth Badreddine is a young female corporate leader with roots in Belgium &amp; Lebanon. She has more than 13 years of corporate experience and has broad knowledge of different domains such as products &amp; services, sales &amp; marketing, strategy &amp; transformation, innovation. She has experience in transforming product portfolios from basic connectivity to digital service providers, innovating traditional telco businesses by introducing adjacent solutions<a class='tooltip-target' data-citationid='7b1a1c95-f3ab-12a1-f9df-8a996de15d41-12-group'>, building &amp; managing partner ecosystems to support growth strategies</a>, and building knowledge &amp; network in 3 different domains (customer care, advertisement &amp; product management) in both B2C and B2B contexts. She is a purpose-driven leader who is energised by genuinely connecting with people<a class='tooltip-target' data-citationid='7b1a1c95-f3ab-12a1-f9df-8a996de15d41-18-group'> and embraces diversity at large</a>. Based on her experience and knowledge, Elizabeth Badreddine can provide a second opinion on product management, product launches, marketing done, leadership development and more

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=29]

Filip Michiels is a great expert to provide a second opinion because he has a proven track record of helping companies navigate major changes and disruptions. With his strategic enterprise view and digital execution/entrepreneurship skills, he can help companies make the shift they need to stay competitive in today’s fast-paced business environment. Filip has a wealth of experience in this area, having worked with many companies across different industries.

He has a deep understanding of what it takes to succeed in today’s digital landscape and can provide valuable insights and guidance to help companies achieve their goals. If you’re looking for someone who can help you navigate change and disruption, Filip Michiels is definitely someone you should consider

&nbsp;

Filip was Datanews CIO of the year 2019

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=40]

Kristien Manteleers is a management consultant with over 20 years of experience as a consultant and as an internal manager/consultant. She started up C the C after her experience and appeals to her network of independent consultants to meet all customer’s requirements. <a class='tooltip-target' data-citationid='24716c17-b294-9802-4b54-1ec251c31226-4-group'>Her style is no-nonsense and her strength is that she dares to ask the question</a>. She is a great expert to provide a second opinion because of her extensive experience in leadership, change, and reskilling.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=17]

Ine Meeussen is a great expert to provide a second opinion on CFO interim and finance outsourcing because she is the founder of UFINITY which provides financial staffing, interim-management, CFO-as-a-service and Anaplan services. She has experience in providing top-tier finance, business, accounting and operational guidance for businesses.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=65]

Pieter Meijlaers is a great expert to provide a second opinion because he is a technology adept and evangelist, product developer and service/experience improver, and creative out-of-the-box thinker<a class='ac-anchor sup-target' href='https://be.linkedin.com/in/pietermeijlaers' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-citationid='f84c0095-b7f3-488a-88d6-50e35a0c0bad-2' aria-label='Pieter Meijlaers - Bedrijfseigenaar - i-ViSiT BV | LinkedIn'><sup>1</sup></a>. His personal motto “Creating Mondriaan out of Kandinsky” shows that he always challenges himself to find a straightforward solution in difficult situations.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=28]

David Ducheyne is an expert in human behavior and strategies. He founded Otolith to help organizations and leaders with their strategies by focusing on human behavior. He believes that both strategy definition and execution are a matter of human behavior. David’s expertise in human behavior makes him a great expert to provide a second opinion on why people do what they do and why they don’t do what they are supposed to do. His experience of more than 25 years of corporate life has given him the knowledge and skills to help organizations and leaders with their strategies. David’s focus on human behavior can help organizations and leaders design, decide, and deliver through purposeful human action

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=27]

Maarten Verschuere is an emerging technology leader and speaker who inspires and enables corporates to surf on new waves of technological enhancement. He has worked as an analytical consultant in retail and FMCG for clients including Tesco and P&amp;G while living in London, Paris and Cincinnati. In 2016, he founded Clever, an AI-driven platform for conversational search which was sold to Zoovu Ltd. in 2019. With his mission to create a better tomorrow by helping companies transform enabled by AI and Web3 technologies, Maarten Verschuere is a great expert to provide a second opinion on how companies can leverage these technologies to transform their businesses. His experience in the industry and his passion for emerging technologies make him an ideal candidate for providing insights into how companies can use AI and Web3 technologies to create a better future.

[booknetic staff=8]

&nbsp;

Horst Remes is a Customer Strategy Expert. He is passionate about helping other leaders make the transition to a customer-centric and operationally efficient organization. Horst Remes believes that nothing is easier to sell than a product or service from a customer-centric company. He has made it his mission to get management teams to create a distinctive and concrete strategy, and arm them against the ever so tempting management bullshit. He goes looking for the arguments behind the opinions. That’s how everyone gets aligned. He has extensive experience in customer-oriented organizations and has expertise in customer-centric processes, customer satisfaction, and customer experience.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=54]

Bjorn Van Reet is a great expert to provide a second opinion because he has a wealth of experience in leadership, vision &amp; strategy, people (HR), innovation, out-of-the-box thinking, architecture, ICT Infrastructure and governance, SOX, ITIL &amp; PRINCE2. He is currently the Chief Information Officer (CIO) at Kinepolis Group<a class='ac-anchor sup-target' href='https://be.linkedin.com/in/bjornvanreet' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-citationid='cb119586-00f3-8a0a-26d5-6dce6f3bd66d-2' aria-label='Bjorn Van Reet - Chief Information Officer (CIO) - Kinepolis - LinkedIn'><sup>1</sup></a>which is a Belgium fast-growing company with an international footprint active in 9 countries. He has been praised by his peers and won the Chief Digital Officer of the Year Awards 2021.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=67]

Geert Vanoverschelde is an expert in events and live communication. He has a wealth of experience in corporate and B2B events, product launches, staff events, congresses and seminars, public events, hospitalities and offsite meetings. He is also an expert in linear and non-linear TV productions including fiction, reality and documentary programs. His expertise in video productions includes corporate films, commercials, social and online video, recruitment video, virals, after movies, branded content &amp; video marketing. Geert Vanoverschelde is a great expert to provide a second opinion because of his vast experience in the field of events and live communication. He has worked on numerous projects and has a deep understanding of the industry. His expertise in linear and non-linear TV productions as well as video productions makes him a valuable asset to any team. Geert Vanoverschelde’s experience and knowledge make him an excellent choice for anyone looking for a second opinion in these areas.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=44]

Bart De Waele is a great expert to provide a second opinion because he has founded some internet companies and is the owner of N-Cube. He is passionate about internet, new technology, communication, transhumanism and entrepreneurship. He is an infovore, saphiofile, gadgetfreak, pattern recognizer and Snow Crash Gargoyle. He has been in business development consulting for years and has over 11K followers on LinkedIn.  He is also a web pioneer who founded Duke &amp; Grace which was formerly known as Netlash.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=21]

Hans Smellinckx is a great expert to provide a second opinion because he has a wealth of experience and knowledge in various fields and industries. He is not only a strategist, but also a change agent, a people manager, an entrepreneur, a marketing and sales leader, a keynote speaker, and a writer. He has worked with big names such as Thomas Cook, Coca-Cola, Ikea, and many others, and has transformed businesses digitally and internally. He has also mentored start-ups and scale-ups through The Birdhouse program, helping them grow from within. He has a global perspective and a passion for innovation and excellence. Hans Smellinckx is the ideal person to give you a fresh and insightful perspective on your business  sales challenges and opportunities.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=51]

Marc Bervoets is an expert in cross-industry negotiations and has been working as a lead business negotiator for large complex arrangements or challenges with existing contracts. He has experience in complex technology delivery roles, diamond client account leadership roles as well as regional DOO roles. With his vast experience and expertise in the field of cross-industry negotiations, he can provide a second opinion that can be trusted and relied upon. His ability to handle complex arrangements and challenges with existing contracts makes him an ideal candidate for providing a second opinion. Marc Bervoets is a great expert who can provide valuable insights and advice that can help you make informed decisions.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=39]

Anette Bohm is a great expert to provide a second opinion because she has more than <strong>30 years</strong> of experience as a proactive and business-minded HR leader. She has steered organizations through complex transitions and built an empowered and talented workforce in cross-cultural environments and highly competitive markets. Her proven expertise in organizational structure and human capital requirements aligns HR functions with business goals, providing the catalyst to optimize performance, enhance productivity, and drive revenue and profit growth. Anette is a forward thinker and articulate communicator with an innate ability to embrace change. Her experience in steering organizations through complex transitions and building an empowered workforce makes her an expert in providing a second opinion.

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=16]

Ilse Vandevyvere is an expert in commercial engineering with a fast-growing track record in marketing, sales &amp; commercial functions. She is passionate about Agile &amp; Emotional Intelligence and loves taking on new business or people challenges. Her customers and team members are what get her happily out of bed in the morning. Her passion for her work is contagious and inspiring. She has a unique ability to see things from different perspectives and provide valuable insights that can help businesses grow and succeed. Her expertise in commercial engineering combined with her passion for Agile &amp; Emotional Intelligence makes her an excellent choice for providing a second opinion. She has a proven track record of success and has helped many businesses achieve their goals.

&nbsp;

Worked before at Proximus

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=33]

Sabine Fannes is a senior HR architect and certified coach with an eye and a heart for people. She is the founder of BeyondYou . Sabine has worked in former executive HR positions at RealDolmen, Clear2Pay, Logica, etc. She has a lot of experience in working like an architect in HR where she analyzes needs, creates plans, determines priorities and work points together with the team, and guides the project until delivery. Sabine is an expert in HR project management and personal/team development. Based on her experience and expertise, Sabine Fannes would be a great expert to provide a second opinion on your HR project .

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=47]

Edwin Van Waes is a great expert to give a second opinion on sales matters. He has a long and successful career in the commercial sector, where he has inspired and motivated teams to get the best out of themselves. He has a result-oriented mentality, where he always strives for high standards, integrity and respect. He leads by example and conveys his enthusiasm and positive mindset to others. He also has a large network of personal contacts, who help him achieve his goals. He is currently commercial director at a company that specializes in IT solutions. He has a degree in industrial sciences: electronics-ICT (industrial engineer) from the University of Antwerp. Edwin Van Waes is someone who knows what he is talking about and who can help you improve your sales performance.

&nbsp;

Former SVP Salesforce and Sales Director SAS

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=71]

Stephane Jacobs is a freelance mobility consultant and fin-tech entrepreneur with a Master’s degree in Transport Economics from the University of Antwerp. He has co-founded several innovative ventures in the fields of mobile parking, electronic meal vouchers, city gift cards and ship-to-shore facilities. He has also been managing director of Mobile-for, an affiliated company of Proximus and leading mobility service provider that offers traffic management and mobile payment solutions for the European market. Before that, he was senior manager at IBM Global Business Services and PWC, where he helped policy and decision makers with strategic decisions in various domains such as business strategy, performance improvement and investment analysis. He has extensive expertise in the public sector, public enterprises and ports, maritime and logistics sectors. Today, he is active as an external advisor of the Flemish Government regarding the transition towards zero emission transportation. Recently, he advised Mastercard regarding their in-car commerce strategy and Parking Brussels regarding their control processes. As an expert, he can provide a good second opinion on any mobility or fin-tech related cases.

His most important expertise, specializations and interests are related to:
• Business Strategy development and Implementation assistance;
• ICT-Strategy development and assistance;
• Audit of public and semi public organizations;
• Performance improvement;
• Process- and programme assistance;
• Investment analysis and socio-economic evaluation of huge investment projects;
• Public and private policy development and -evaluation;
• Preparation of alternative financing solutions;
• Location advise.
His market segment expertise is:
• The public sector domain (Benelux, Flemish and federal government);
• Public enterprises in transition;
• Ports, maritime and logistics sector.

Specialties: Transport &amp; (e)Mobility, Mobile Payments &amp; Fin-Tech start-ups

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=1]
<div id='ConnectiveDocSignExtentionInstalled' data-extension-version='1.0.4'></div>

Stijn Vander Plaetse is a former vice president and CEO with over two decades of experience in the telecommunications, cloud and IT industry. He has led both retail and wholesale businesses in developing and implementing effective marketing and corporate strategies that resulted in increased revenue and customer satisfaction. He has also transformed and repositioned several companies and organizations to cope with changing market dynamics and customer expectations. He is an optimistic and driven professional who sees every challenge as an opportunity and who strives to balance the interests of customers, employees and companies. He values knowledge sharing and teamwork as key factors for success. He is an expert who can offer a refreshing second opinion on any marketing or corporate strategy related issues in the telecommunications, cloud or IT sector. His extensive experience, combined with his straightforward approach to business and his ability to provide valuable insights and recommendations, make him a reliable partner and a valuable asset to any organization seeking sustainable growth

[booknetic staff=3]

&nbsp;

Isabel de Clercq is een geweldige expert om een tweede mening te geven over verschillende onderwerpen die te maken hebben met werk, welzijn en innovatie. Ze heeft meer dan 25 jaar ervaring als sales manager, change manager en content marketeer oa bij Wolters Kluwer België<a class='ac-anchor sup-target' href='https://readmylips.be/sprekers/isabel-de-clercq' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-citationid='487aaafd-d96a-4bea-3d92-61e0a3d3a87e-2' aria-label='Isabel De Clercq | Read my lips'><sup>1</sup></a>. Ze is ook de auteur van verschillende boeken: Sproet, Gekruld en Het hybride werken. Ze is een veelgevraagd spreker over topics als kennisdeling, asynchrone samenwerking en het Hybride Werken<a class='ac-anchor sup-target' href='https://readmylips.be/sprekers/isabel-de-clercq' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-citationid='487aaafd-d96a-4bea-3d92-61e0a3d3a87e-6' aria-label='Isabel De Clercq | Read my lips'><sup>1</sup></a>. Ze combineert een verfrissende visie met praktische oplossingen en een aanstekelijke enthousiasme. Ze weet hoe ze mensen kan inspireren en motiveren om anders te werken en te leren. Ze is niet bang om clichés onderuit te halen en een stevige ‘kick in the ass’ te geven<sup>1</sup>. Isabel de Clercq is de ideale persoon om u te helpen uw organisatie naar een hoger niveau te tillen

&nbsp;

https://www.connectsharelead.com

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=23]

Ulrik Van Schepdael is an expert in his field with a broad technology background and business acumen that drives and manages the success of an ICT company. He is an effective communicator who is creative and target-oriented. His specialties include leading high-tech businesses, managing the 4 P’s, innovation management, and strategic agility. Ulrik’s expertise in these areas makes him an ideal candidate to provide a second opinion. His ability to communicate effectively and his creativity make him a valuable asset to any team. Ulrik’s target-oriented approach ensures that he always delivers results that exceed expectations. His broad technology background combined with his business acumen makes him a valuable asset to any organization. Ulrik Van Schepdael is truly an expert in his field and a great choice for anyone seeking a second opinion

&nbsp;

[booknetic staff=14]
